  "query_preview": "/Through Tuesday/...\nIssued at 228 AM MDT Wed Sep 9 2026\n\nFor today, drier in westerly flow aloft will be over the area as a \ncold front move across the plains early this mornng.  As a result, \nexpect dry conditions with cooler temps as highs finally drop back \nto more seasonal levels.\n\nBy tonight, the flow aloft will become more WNW as low level \nsoutheast flow develops which will lead to some return of moisture \nacross the east central plains.  Meanwhile, a weak disturbance \nembedded in WNW flow will combine with warm air advection and bring \nsome nocturnal tstms, to portions of the sern plains overnight. \nCurrent data still keeps most of this activity over sern CO, with\nsrn Lincoln county, being on the nrn fringe. For now have kept in\nchc pops mainly across srn portions of Lincoln county overnight.\n\nOn Thu, the flow aloft will remain WNW as southerly level flow is \nacross the plains.  MLCAPE will rise up to 1000 j/kg over portions \nof the plains by aftn.  For now, chances for tstms stll look on the \nlow side as I can't find a focus for activity. However, can't rule \nout an isold storm or two across Lincoln and Washington counties. \nMeanwhile, temps will begin to warm as readings reach the upper 80's \nto lower 90's over nern CO.\n\nLooking ahead to Fri, zonal flow aloft will be over the area as a \nsfc lee trough develops over the plains.  This will lead to another \nwarm day as highs rise into the upper 80's to mid 90's over the \nplains.  Meanwhile, models have some mid level moisture embedded in \nthe flow, which may lead to a slight chc of higher based \nshowers/tstms over the higher terrain.  Across the plains, MLCAPE is \nrather minimal so chances of precip look low.\n\nFor Fri night into Sat, zonal flow aloft will continue.  Meanwhile, \na cold front will move across Fri night into Sat morning.  This \nfront will drop temps back to more seasonal levels across nern CO. \nMLCAPE is fcst to be in the 500-800 j/kg across the plains with \nlower values across the higher terrain. Thus will keep in a \nslight chc for showers/tstms across the area for the aftn/early \nevening hours.\n\nBy Sun, an upper level trough will move into the nrn Rockies with \nincreasing WSW flow aloft across the area.  At the sfc, a lee trough \nwill intensify east of the mtns with southerly low level flow across \nthe plains.  MLCAPE is fcst to increase to 1000-1500 j/kg over \nportions of the the plains east of a pseudo dryline.  Thus may see a \nfew stronger storms by late aftn thru the evening hours.  Highs on \nSun, will likely rise back to above normal levels.\n\nLooking ahead to Mon, rather dry WSW flow aloft will be over the \nareas a cool front moves across the plains Sun night into Mon \nmorning.  Latest data still doesn't show much low level moisture \nbehind the front, so it may end up being dry with temps dropping \nback to seasonal normals.",
